From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: never replace a known AP-MLD attribution with nothing

agent_init_interfaces() tears the AP-MLD's affiliated-AP attribution down
unconditionally:

	list_for_each_entry(ap, &re->aplist, list) {
		ap->torndown = true;
		ap->enabled = false;
		if (ap->is_affiliated_ap)
			mld_del_ap(a, ap);

apmld_parse() then rebuilds it, but every link has to pass a band gate first,
and the empty case re-arms the teardown:

	if (mld->num_affiliated_ap == 0) {
		agnt_info(LOG_MLO, "%s: no affiliated APs found in MLD, schedule reload\n", ...);
		timer_set(&a->init_ifaces_scheduler, IFACE_TIMEOUT * 1000);
	}

Unconditional teardown, gated refill, and a failure path that schedules another
teardown. Once the gate starts failing the set can only stay at zero, and the
node keeps reporting an AP-MLD with no affiliated APs while it is demonstrably
running three links - iw dev ap-mld-1 info shows ch1 + ch36 + ch37 and
/var/run/hostapd/ holds ap-mld-1_link0..2 the whole time.

Measured on bpi-4g, 2026-07-22, sampling what the agent reports right after a
map-agent restart:

	t=0    0      (before the restart)
	t=15   3      populated
	t=60   3
	t=90   0      emptied by itself
	t=150  0      and never comes back

The controller stores what it is told, so mapc.db ends up with an apmld row
carrying num_ap=0 and affiliated_ap / ttlm holding only the nodes whose
attribution has not been re-run yet. Every affiliated_ap=6 / ttlm=48 reading so
far was taken inside that ~60 s window after something restarted map-agent, not
in steady state.

Keep the last attribution that produced links, and fall back to it when a
rebuild comes out empty. A later rebuild that produces anything at all replaces
it wholesale, so genuine removals still land; the only transition that stops
being representable is the one that is never legitimate - a running MLD
reporting nothing. The kept_prev_ap flag keeps this to one log line per
transition in each direction, because the path runs on every init pass while
the gate stays shut.

This is the discipline 961-radio-reconcile-sweep already applies to radios, and
the one the bss table still needs.

Not 971 (patches/unmerged/): that one restructures attribution into a periodic
async refresh, and was abandoned because the blocking round-trip it existed for
was solved a layer down in libwifi under ADR 0009. This is 12 lines in the
existing synchronous path and touches no async machinery.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/mld.h
+++ b/src/mld.h
@@ -45,6 +45,15 @@
 #define MAX_AFFILIATED_AP_LINKS_NUM 14
         uint8_t affiliated_ap[MAX_AFFILIATED_AP_LINKS_NUM][6];
 
+	/* PATCH 983: the last attribution that produced links, and whether we
+	 * are currently running on it. agent_init_interfaces() tears the
+	 * affiliated set down unconditionally while the refill below is gated
+	 * on band, so without a fallback a single failed gate empties the set
+	 * for the lifetime of the process. */
+	int num_last_good_ap;
+	uint8_t last_good_ap[MAX_AFFILIATED_AP_LINKS_NUM][6];
+	bool kept_prev_ap;
+
 	struct list_head list;
 };
 
--- a/src/mld.c
+++ b/src/mld.c
@@ -463,7 +463,53 @@
 			break;
 		}
 
-		if (mld->num_affiliated_ap == 0) {
+		/* PATCH 983: never replace a known set with nothing.
+		 *
+		 * The teardown above is unconditional, this refill is gated on band,
+		 * and the empty case re-arms the teardown by scheduling another init
+		 * pass. Once the gate starts failing the set can therefore only stay
+		 * at zero, and a node keeps reporting an AP-MLD with no affiliated
+		 * APs while it is demonstrably running three links. Measured on
+		 * bpi-4g 2026-07-22: populated for ~60 s after a map-agent restart,
+		 * then zero for good.
+		 *
+		 * Keep the last attribution that produced links instead. A later
+		 * attribution that produces anything at all replaces it wholesale, so
+		 * genuine removals still land; only the transition that is never
+		 * legitimate - a running MLD reporting nothing - stops existing.
+		 */
+		if (mld->num_affiliated_ap > 0) {
+			mld->num_last_good_ap = mld->num_affiliated_ap;
+			memcpy(mld->last_good_ap, mld->affiliated_ap,
+			       sizeof(mld->last_good_ap));
+			if (mld->kept_prev_ap) {
+				agnt_warn(LOG_MLO, "%s: %s: attribution recovered, %d affiliated APs\n",
+					  __func__, mld->ifname, mld->num_affiliated_ap);
+				mld->kept_prev_ap = false;
+			}
+		} else if (mld->num_last_good_ap > 0) {
+			int k;
+
+			memcpy(mld->affiliated_ap, mld->last_good_ap,
+			       sizeof(mld->affiliated_ap));
+			mld->num_affiliated_ap = mld->num_last_good_ap;
+			for (k = 0; k < mld->num_affiliated_ap; k++) {
+				struct netif_ap *prev;
+
+				prev = agent_get_ap(a, mld->affiliated_ap[k]);
+				if (prev)
+					prev->is_affiliated_ap = true;
+			}
+			/* Logged once per transition: this path runs on every init pass
+			 * while the gate stays shut, and a line per pass would bury the
+			 * ring buffer it is meant to be visible in. */
+			if (!mld->kept_prev_ap) {
+				agnt_warn(LOG_MLO, "%s: %s: attribution came out empty, keeping the previous %d affiliated APs\n",
+					  __func__, mld->ifname, mld->num_affiliated_ap);
+				mld->kept_prev_ap = true;
+			}
+			timer_set(&a->init_ifaces_scheduler, IFACE_TIMEOUT * 1000);
+		} else {
 			agnt_info(LOG_MLO, "%s: no affiliated APs found in MLD, schedule reload\n", __func__);
 			timer_set(&a->init_ifaces_scheduler, IFACE_TIMEOUT * 1000);
 		}
